# Refusals: a form wap does not take, reported at the user's line (notes/wap.md).
#
# Every stage refuses through here, never with a bare `raise`, so every message has the same shape and points where
# the program wrote the form, whichever stage found it (core/stage.wap carries the positions there):
#
#   line 2:1: the emitter takes no call but print of a text yet: print 3
#
# Later: the readings a phrase allows, a fix-it, and the rule that expanded the form.

refused(n: Node, why: text) := raise place_of(n) + why + ": " + n

# `line 2:1: `, or nothing for a node without a position
place_of(n: Node) as text := if line_of(n) == ø then "" else "line ${line_of(n)}:${column_of(n)}: "
